  - model discontinuity
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - human-AI co-creation
abstract: >
  This paper introduces Knowledge Continuity Engineering (KCE), a proposed
  discipline that treats knowledge continuity as a first-class engineering
  concern. We identify five core problems (model discontinuity, human
  discontinuity, provenance decay, semantic drift, authority fragmentation),
  propose seven design principles and a five-layer reference architecture,
  and describe BRIDGRAI as a working reference implementation developed
  over 3.5 years.
repository-code: "https://github.com/amidigiart/kce-framework"
